# @NAME@ wiki — consumer skill

You have access to a bundled wiki of @PAGE_COUNT@ pages covering background knowledge for **@NAME@**. Use it when you need a settled fact, a canonical code pattern, or a standard convention in this domain — **before** doing a web search.

## Scope

@SCOPE_SUMMARY@

See `MANIFEST.md` for the full scope summary, page counts by type, and the curator's top-topics index. See `wiki/out_of_scope.md` for what is deliberately not covered.

## How to use

All three commands live in this skill's `bin/` directory and require nothing but POSIX shell:

- `bin/wiki-manifest` — orient: print the wiki's manifest with top topics
- `bin/wiki-search <query>` — find pages by title, tag, or body content
  - `--type concept|convention|code-pattern|claim|source|entity` filters by type
  - `--n N` caps results (default 10)
- `bin/wiki-read <slug>` — read a page; backlinks (grouped by edge type) appended at the end
  - `--no-backlinks` suppresses the backlink block

Less common:

- `bin/wiki-list [--tag T] [--type T] [--prefix P]` — enumerate pages with optional filters
- `bin/wiki-backlinks [--type EDGE] <slug>` — show pages linking to `<slug>` as `<edge>: <from>` lines

## When to use this wiki vs. live retrieval

**Use the wiki for:**
- Definitions, conventions, dataset formats, evaluation protocols
- Canonical code patterns (with citation back to repo + commit + line range)
- Settled empirical claims with evidence trails

**Use live retrieval (web search, arxiv) for:**
- Anything published in the last 30 days
- Fast-moving leaderboards or SOTA scores
- Novel investigation, hypothesis generation
- Anything explicitly listed in `wiki/out_of_scope.md`

## Edge types in backlinks

Five edge types may appear. `references` (the default, from prose `[[wikilinks]]`) is the most common; the others are typed relationships that often matter more:

- `extends` — A builds on B's foundation
- `contradicts` — A asserts something incompatible with B
- `supersedes` — A replaces B; B is obsolete
- `implements` — A is a realization of the concept/convention B

When `wiki-read` shows typed backlinks, treat them as load-bearing. A page with three `contradicts:` backlinks is contested; one with `supersedes:` backlinks may be the old version.

## Feedback

Append observations to `feedback.md` at the root of this skill: gaps you noticed, claims that turned out wrong, pages that surprised you with their accuracy. The curator harvests this periodically and routes items back into ingest or the explorer queue.

